/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A neurodevelopmental disorder, autism spectrum disorder \(ASD\) is defined by sustained limitations in social communication and interaction, and by stereotyped forms of behavior, interests, or activities. An elevated excitationinhibition ratio has been documented across multiple areas as the hippocampus, a structure critically involved in spatial orientation, episodic recall, and emotional regulation. A crucial stage in development involves the alteration in GABA's influence, transitioning from excitatory to inhibitory. Animal models of autism exhibit a delayed "chloride switch", linked to intracellular chloride, which is mantained by the activity of the Na+K+Cl- cotransporter 1 \(NKCC1\). In this work we studied the participation of NKCC1 on synaptic plasticity in the dentate gyrus of the valproate \(VPA\) model of autism, a region that acts as a filter of information from cortical inputs. We observe the existence of a NKCC1- dependent component of EPSP which is higher in VPA group. Both AMPA and NMDA components of EPSP are dependent on NKCC1 activity. The application of four high frecuency stimulation pulses induced a robust LTP, which has a presynaptic component due to presynaptic mechanisms. Animals exposed to VPA displayed enhanced LTP levels in contrast to the control group, whereas the external application of bumetanide reverted these levels to those characteristic of control animals, implying NKCC1's contribution to this augmented plasticity. Altogether, our results suggest that in the VPA model both the size of EPSP and the induction of LTP depends on the activity of NKCC1 cotransporter, potentially due to a depolarizing or even excitatory effect of GABA. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
